cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "Dissemination-aware weather forecast vintages for day-ahead electricity price forecasting in Japan"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Okauchi"
    given-names: "Ryota"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5391-7133"
    affiliation: "The University of Tokyo"
    website: "https://github.com/R-Okauchi"
  - family-names: "Chun"
    given-names: "Pang-jo"
    affiliation: "The University of Tokyo"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction companion for a study of how the DISSEMINATION time of a weather
  forecast -- not its initialisation time -- determines what that forecast is
  worth in a day-ahead electricity market. Japan's meso-scale model reaches
  users about 2 h 16 min after initialisation (the median, measured here from
  881 days of
  archive timestamps, so the previous-day 00 UTC run arrives after the 10:00 JST
  JEPX gate that an initialisation-time reading would admit. Rebuilding the
  evaluation as a dissemination-correct ladder of run-pinned tiers, the
  repository carries one script per analysis phase, a frozen provenance JSON per
  phase, and a drift guard that re-derives every headline quantity in the
  manuscript from that provenance without needing raw data.
keywords:
  - electricity price forecasting
  - forecast vintage
  - gate closure
  - dissemination time
  - value of information
  - imbalance settlement
  - solar curtailment
  - price floor
  - JEPX
  - equivalence testing
  - pre-registration
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/UT-Team-Chun/forecast-vintage-epf"
